    [Feature][Quantization] Backport ModelSlim W4A8 dynamic Linear support to v0.32.0rc (#20507)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Backport the ModelSlim W4A8 dynamic Linear support from
    [#20469](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/pull/20469) to the
    `releases/v0.32.0rc` branch. This enables ModelSlim `W4A8_DYNAMIC`
    Linear layers with symmetric per-channel INT4 weights and dynamic
    per-token INT8 activations, including packed checkpoint loading, TP
    scale-bias reduction, and the A8W4 grouped-matmul path. Small TP output
    partitions retain ND layout when they do not meet INT4 NZ alignment;
    fused-MoE weights retain explicit NZ conversion.
    
    The backport is based directly on the official `releases/v0.32.0rc`
    branch. Qwen3.8 Flash-Next support from #16981 is already present in
    this release branch and is not duplicated here.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. Users can load ModelSlim `W4A8_DYNAMIC` Linear weights with
    symmetric per-channel INT4 weights and per-token INT8 activations.
    Per-group INT and non-ModelSlim checkpoints are rejected by this Linear
    scheme. Existing MXFP schemes are outside this change.
    
    Release note: `release_notes/fragments/20507.yaml`.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - The W4A8 CPU unit-test changes from #20469 are included, covering
    packed weight shape, TP partition constraints, NZ alignment, scale bit
    encoding and bias reduction, asymmetric-offset rejection, empty input,
    and prepared-input protection.
    - The patch was assembled by applying the two W4A8 implementation
    commits and the test commit from #20469 onto `releases/v0.32.0rc`
    without conflicts.
    - NPU service startup, accuracy, and performance validation on the
    0.32.0rc environment remain pending.
    
    ### Checklist
    
    - [x] Boundary / edge-case coverage
    - [x] Regression test
    - [x] Error / failure path coverage
    - [x] Meaningful & reliable tests
    - [ ] Performance impact: hardware benchmarks remain pending.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/544f182d9f0c9bfe8bd7645525951d5e3692a542
    
